(Corridor Agreement expires with no renewal) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P1] Notice from the Realm Trade Ministry. The Corridor Agreement expired on 10) Tj
T*
(September 2026.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P2] Talks on renewal ended without agreement. No replacement arrangement has) Tj
T*
(been signed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P3] From the day after expiry, wheat and maize leaving Orvan Grain Port by sea) Tj
T*
(move under the general export rules.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P4] The ministry advises exporters to read the general rules before booking) Tj
T*
(cargoes. The port remains open.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P5] The notice is signed by the trade ministry's corridor desk and takes effect) Tj
T*
(on expiry. Exporters who hold bookings made under the agreement should ask their) Tj
T*
(agents to confirm the terms that now apply. The ministry says the general rules) Tj
T*
(are already published and that no transitional quota has been created. Shipping) Tj
T*
(lines have been told to expect the same customs checks as any other grain cargo.) Tj
T*
(The port authority will report loadings in the usual monthly return.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P6] The corridor desk will keep a record of bookings made before expiry so that) Tj
T*
(any cargo already under contract can be traced. Exporters who need a copy of the) Tj
T*
(old terms may request one from the ministry. The notice does not create a grace) Tj
T*
(period and does not reopen the agreement. It applies to wheat and maize alike,) Tj
T*
(and to every buyer that used the sea route.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
([P7] A further notice will follow if the position changes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
